From: ReadyNAS NG <readynasng@build>
Subject: [PATCH 22/23] padre_gmac: NAPI, GRO and receive checksum by the engine

Receive and transmit completion move from the hard interrupt to a NAPI
poll: the interrupt masks the M4 engine and schedules the poll, which
cleans the transmit ring, receives up to the budget through
napi_gro_receive (buffers from napi_alloc_skb) and unmasks.

The GMT block of the DJ engine checks the TCP/UDP checksum of received
IPv4 frames (GMAC_CTRL bit 22, GMT mode 4, result in bits 17-22 of the
descriptor, as in the 2.6.17 driver): good frames that are not IP
fragments get CHECKSUM_UNNECESSARY (ethtool -K rx); the others go to the
stack, which checks them. padre_gmac.csum_verify=1 (also in
/sys/module/padre_gmac/parameters) checks every frame in software and
counts disagreements; ethtool -S shows the counters.

No transmit checksum nor scatter-gather: through the engine's meta
command descriptors, the checksum state of the engine drifted from the
one the driver asked for (seed sent unfilled, ICMP checksum zeroed).

Measured on the NAS (500 MB over SMB3 from a PC on Wi-Fi): unsigned
write 9.0 MiB/s and 0.10-0.12 CPU s/MiB instead of 6.2-7.5 MiB/s and
0.13-0.15; read unchanged (bound by the transmit path).
